{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/84328-extra-mummy-books","id":84328,"title":"Extra Mummy Books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-04T18:58:46-08:00","id":84328,"title":"Extra Mummy Books","content":"So, with an eye towards running a Mummy game sometime in the next few months, I was wondering if there were any recommended books that would be good for fleshing out the Mummy setting with its current dearth of specifically Mummy-related books. I've grabbed Reliquary, and of course I have the corebook and Guildhalls of the Deathless. Would the Book of the Dead be a good choice? A lot of Mummy powers interact with ghosts, so I was planning on using them pretty extensively. And are there any other blue books that people would recommend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T21:19:20-08:00","id":84371,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't recommend Book of the Dead since it posits an Underworld very different from Duat. <br /> <br /> I recommend Second Sight as a good resource for mortal cultists who also dip into a bit of sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T22:06:01-08:00","id":84392,"title":"","content":"Antagonists has a pretty nice section on cult, how they operate, who joins, brainwashing, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T04:40:37-08:00","id":84504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/84328-extra-mummy-books?p=84371#post84371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't recommend Book of the Dead since it posits an Underworld very different from Duat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, on the other hand, do recommend the <i>Book of the Dead</i> as it does have some interesting things for ghosts, which Mummies are very in tune with. Its Underworld doesn't diminish the themes of Duat anymore than using the Underworld in a Mage game would undermine Stygia.<br /> <br /> You have to be careful, of course, but it would be fun to throw your players off. As the GM you might decide there's no relationship, and the PCs call into question the nature of the universe, or you might decide Duat is part of the Underworld, which might be a good basis for a late-game Apotheosis kind of story. Perhaps it's a dead dominion, or a realm even beneath the ocean of fragments; perhaps the Judges are the deathlords, or perhaps they're greater or lesser than them.<br /> <br /> I do intend for my PC to journey in the upper reaches and I think it'll turn out fun.<br /> <br /> It's your game, so make it what you want!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T13:50:01-08:00","id":84820,"title":"","content":"Although I haven't read the Book of the Dead yet, if what I've read about it is correct (that is to say, that at the bottom of the Underworld is a lake where you lose parts of yourself, and that the further into the Underworld you go the older the ghosts are) then the Underworld as-is has some pretty appropriate themes for Mummy. Putting Duat at the bottom of the lake would be a pretty handy way of describing why and how Mummies lose Memory at the start of each descent, for example.<br /> <br /> I'll have to look into Second Sight and Antagonists. They sound like they could be pretty good reads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T13:59:35-08:00","id":84825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/84328-extra-mummy-books?p=84820#post84820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I haven't read the Book of the Dead yet, if what I've read about it is correct (that is to say, that at the bottom of the Underworld is a lake where you lose parts of yourself, and that the further into the Underworld you go the older the ghosts are) then the Underworld as-is has some pretty appropriate themes for Mummy. Putting Duat at the bottom of the lake would be a pretty handy way of describing why and how Mummies lose Memory at the start of each descent, for example.<br /> <br /> I'll have to look into Second Sight and Antagonists. They sound like they could be pretty good reads.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ocean of Fragments isn't so much the <i>bottom</i> (I'm doubtful that Tartarus <i>has</i> a bottom) as it is the deepest anyone's ever gone and come back. Word from the writers is that &quot;Gone&quot; - one of the scenarios in WoD: Urban Legends' sixth chapter - is connected to the Ocean; one of the variants the section presents concerns torpid vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T21:01:36-08:00","id":85069,"title":"","content":"Right, it does really sound like I should get this book. Sticking Duat below the Ocean of Fragments doesn't sound too unreasonable. It doesn't even need to come up in-game, but tying the Underworld to Mummy mythology in the back of my head makes for a solid justification of using the Underworld in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T03:57:37-07:00","id":87403,"title":"","content":"I think there was a Domain in the book that seemed to emulate, although weirdly, what this thread is talking about. I think the Domain is called Mictlan (?) and as a guardian, the land has someone who greatly resembles Anpu. If the Arisen somehow end up there on a relic hunt, they may be astonished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T04:39:51-07:00","id":87421,"title":"","content":"Heh. I've actually been a bit distracted by Block by Bloody Block, which I grabbed pretty much on a whim. Looks like a great way to represent different mummies and their cults (not to mention other factions like Last Dynasty International) vying for control over certain parts of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}